# Northstar Services Travel and Expense Policy

**Version:** 4.2 **Effective:** 1 July 2026 **Owner:** Dana Whitfield, Controller
**Questions:** ap-help@northstar.example

*Fictional policy for training use only.*

## 1. Purpose and scope

1.1 This policy covers business expenses paid personally by Northstar employees and claimed for reimbursement.
1.2 It applies to all employees in all offices. Amounts are in the currency of the employee's home office (USD for Chicago and Denver, CAD for Toronto).

## 2. Submitting a claim

2.1 Submit claims in the expense system within **30 days** of the expense date.
2.2 Claims submitted after 30 days need written approval from your manager. Claims older than **90 days** are not reimbursed.
2.3 Your manager approves every claim. Claims over **2,500** in total also need CFO approval.

## 3. Receipts

3.1 An itemised receipt is required for every expense of **25 or more**.
3.2 If a receipt is lost, complete the Missing Receipt Declaration and have your manager sign it. You may use this for no more than **three** expenses per calendar year.
3.3 Credit card statements alone are not accepted as receipts.

## 4. Meals

4.1 Daily meal limit while travelling: **75** domestic, **100** international. The limit covers breakfast, lunch and dinner together.
4.2 Amounts above the daily limit are not reimbursed unless your manager approves an exception in writing before the claim is submitted.
4.3 Meals are not reimbursed when you are not travelling, except under section 7.
4.4 Tips up to **20%** of the meal cost are reimbursable and count toward the daily limit.

## 5. Lodging

5.1 Hotel limit: **250** per night before taxes. In New York, San Francisco, London and Toronto the limit is **325** per night.
5.2 Book through the company travel portal where available.
5.3 Room upgrades, minibar charges, in-room movies and laundry for trips shorter than five nights are not reimbursed.

## 6. Transport

6.1 Air travel is economy class for flights under **six hours**. Premium economy is allowed for flights of six hours or more.
6.2 Personal car mileage is reimbursed at **0.67 per mile** (USD offices) or **0.70 per km** (Toronto). Commuting between home and your usual office is not reimbursed.
6.3 Taxis and ride-share are reimbursed for business travel. Receipts follow section 3.
6.4 Parking and tolls on business trips are reimbursed. Parking fines and traffic tickets are not.

## 7. Client entertainment

7.1 Meals and events with clients are reimbursed when they have a clear business purpose. List the attendees and their companies on the claim.
7.2 Client entertainment over **500** in total needs your department head's approval **before** the event.
7.3 Alcohol is reimbursed only as part of approved client entertainment, and never more than **30%** of the total bill.

## 8. Gifts

8.1 Gifts to clients are limited to **100** per person per calendar year.
8.2 Cash and gift cards are never allowed as client gifts.

## 9. Not reimbursable

9.1 Personal entertainment, including films, spa services and gym fees.
9.2 Fines and penalties of any kind.
9.3 Expenses for family members or guests who are not on business.
9.4 Membership fees for clubs or airline lounges.

## 10. Exceptions

10.1 Only the Controller may interpret this policy or grant an exception not described above. Send requests to ap-help@northstar.example.
